course: dictionary
lesson: 10741
title: Upstream: against the flow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Upstream means towards the source of a river, the place where it begins, and against the way the water flows. Rivers run downhill, so going upstream is like swimming up a slope made of moving water.
explain: «Salmon swim upstream from the sea to the river where they hatched.» The fish push against the current to get back to the place where they were born. The word upstream tells you the direction they are going.
explain: Upstream can also describe a place. «Upstream of the bridge» means further up the river than the bridge, nearer its source. Downstream is the opposite: nearer the mouth, where the river meets the sea.
explain: Upstream can be used in an informal way too. Swimming upstream means doing something hard that goes against what most people do or want. You can use context clues to work out which meaning fits.
fact: Upstream means towards the source of a river, against the way the water flows.
fact: The source is upstream, and the mouth is downstream.
fact: Upstream can be an adverb, as in «row upstream», or an adjective, as in an upstream place.
fact: Informal: «swimming upstream» means doing something hard, against what most people do or want.
fact: Pollution upstream can flow downstream and affect places further down the river.
exercise: «Salmon swim upstream from the sea to the river where they hatched.» Which way are the salmon going? | Across the river from bank to bank | *Against the flow, towards the place where the river starts | Down the river, with the water
exercise: «Upstream of the bridge» is a place. Where is it? | *Further up the river than the bridge, nearer its source | Across the road from the bridge | Under the bridge
exercise: Sam practises the piano every day while his friends play games. Why might someone say Sam is «swimming upstream»? | He is going to the beach | *He is doing something hard against what most people do | He is swimming in a river
test: «In autumn brown bears gather at rivers to catch salmon swimming upstream.» What are the salmon doing? | Sleeping on the bottom of the river | *Swimming against the flow of the river | Floating lazily down with the current | Hiding under the bank
test: «The Mole cannot bear to go to bed, so the two friends row upstream in the dark.» Which way are they rowing? | *Against the flow of the river, towards its source | With the water, down towards the sea | Round in a circle on the lake | Backwards to the start
exam: «A weir keeps the water deep upstream for boats.» Which place is upstream of the weir? | The bank behind the boats | The water below the wall, where it churns round and round | *The water on the side the river flows from, further up | The river's mouth, where it meets the sea
